title: Running shipped scripts
tags: [[Scripting the GUI]]
kind: guide
summary: script:run lists the scripts installed with the configuration and runs the one you pick; its output goes to the message panel and it shows in the task bar until it ends.


<<key "script:run" "g s">> (`script:run`) opens the command input on the list of
installed scripts, each with its one-line description; pick one and it runs.

```
:script:run gui-tag-folder
```

The name alone works too, with or without `.sh` — which is how a script is bound to a
key ([[Keybindings]]).

!! What is listed

The scripts are files of the configuration, in `~/.config/metafolder/scripts/`
([[The configuration repository]]). A script is ''offered'' when it is a `.sh` file
directly in that directory whose leading comment block has a line

```
# Summary: Bulk-apply one tag over a query's metarecords (yes/no/mixed walk).
```

The text after `Summary:` is the description shown. A file without that line is a
helper the others source — `gui-tag-next.sh`, everything under `lib/` — and is not
listed. The directory is read at each launch: a script of your own, dropped there with
a `# Summary:` line, is offered at once, with no restart ([[Writing a GUI script]]).

The shipped ones are listed in [[Shipped script]].

!! While it runs

The script is run as `bash <path>`, ''without arguments'': a shipped script asks in
the GUI for what it was not given — a tag, a folder, which set to act on
([[A query is the scope]]).

* Its output, and its exit code when not zero, go to the message log of the workspace it was launched from; the focused slot switches to the [[message panel]] unless that workspace already shows it.
* It shows in the task bar under its file name, spinning while it works and still while it waits for you ([[Status bar and task bar]]).
* Its questions appear in a bar above the status line, and Escape stops it ([[Script sessions]]).
* A script that fails says so in red on the status bar of the workspace it was launched from: ''gui-tag-folder.sh failed (exit 1)''.
* A script you stopped says ''gui-tag-folder.sh stopped'' there, not in red: a stop you asked for is not a failure.

!! From a terminal

The same files run from a shell while the GUI is open, and there they take arguments:

```
bash ~/.config/metafolder/scripts/gui-tag-folder.sh music/jazz 'mfr_path =>* "/albums"'
```

They are installed without the execute bit, hence `bash`. Started this way a script is
not known to the GUI: no task-bar entry, and its questions belong to no workspace, so
they stay on screen whatever tab is shown. Escape cannot stop it — it closes the
question instead, which every shipped script takes as ''stop''.
